From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:36:24 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] SWGL GPU path: loops that do not fit go to the CPU quad by
 quad

WebRender scales a blur's source down only when the deviation is large on
both axes, so a one-direction blur can need more steps than a 9_3 pixel
shader can unroll. The unrolled loop then stopped early, and the result
came out faint (dirty-rect-blur-*, filter-blur-scaled-xonly).

For loops of the form `for (int i = c; i <= B; i += s)`, where B comes from
flat varyings (through locals and min()), glsl-to-cxx now emits the
condition under which the loop fits the unroll limit as gpu_accept(limit).
The build records which limit the chosen pixel shader was unrolled to.
Before a GPU draw, SWGL runs the vertex stage for each quad and asks. One
refusal sends the draw to the CPU, where it is shaded and then placed by
the GPU. A limit of 12 is tried between 16 and 8.

SWGL_GPU_CPU=<substring> keeps matching programs on the CPU, for testing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
